number here is from a `GGML_VK_FORCE_MMVQ=1` arm. The original evidence, unchanged and still the reason the `0` path exists (added 2026-09-10, lane-230/R46 commit C): **MEASURED, MIXED, which is why it shipped OFF then.** RIG-A, `test-backend-ops`, 3 interleaved rounds per arm in one quiet hold, base = the unchanged kernel, candidate = commit C on top of the gated commit B2 (`32-paired-c.txt`, 96 cells, raw timings in `32-paired-c.json`). **Against the SHIPPED kernel it loses at `n=7` on three of four primary 27B shapes** - `-28.37%` (4096x14336), `-26.13%` (17408x5120), `-13.29%` (5120x17408) - **raw rounds non-overlapping**, so repeatable, not noise. The PREREG promotion bar (>5% median at `n=1..4`, no >3% repeatable regression on any primary shape) is also missed at `n=4`, 4096x14336: `-6.85%` against B2 (DERIVED, cross-session). **Where it wins it wins large**: 248320x5120 `+38.00 / +45.73 / +46.43 / +51.79%` at `n=1..4` against the unchanged kernel, `+94.85%` at `n=6`. A per-width admit was REFUSED as overfitting - the winning region is one shape at two widths. The `n=7` cliff is **non-monotonic** (`+13.69 / -13.88 / +17.68%` at `n=6/7/8` on 5120x17408 against B2), which points at a `NUM_COLS == 7` tail defect in the mmvq framework rather than a tuning loss; that is where a narrowed admit must start. Routing was proven by a **planted-RED in commit C's dot product only**: with the env unset every `sx8` MUL_MAT case is green, with `=1` ten of twelve go red and the two `mul_mm` cases stay green. Evidence: `research/local-inference/lane-evidence/2026-09-10-lane-230-r46-sx8-mmv/`. |
